WEBVTT

00:00:01.456 --> 00:00:08.037
Candy realized that taking care
of children is hard work.

00:00:09.412 --> 00:00:14.088
She realized that she ought to study
more and become a good person.

00:00:14.616 --> 00:00:19.768
Thus, Candy went on a journey across
the ocean to study in London.

00:00:20.323 --> 00:00:26.637
Love transcends raging waves.

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:35.679
The trip to England has extended
for many days already.

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:50.981
What's the matter, Kurin?

00:00:54.282 --> 00:00:55.505
Something happened?

00:01:00.431 --> 00:01:02.398
A seagull fell onto the deck.

00:01:06.432 --> 00:01:08.870
Kurin, so that's why you called me?

00:01:12.268 --> 00:01:14.553
Poor thing, you are hurt...

00:01:28.365 --> 00:01:30.570
Is there a doctor amongst you?

00:01:31.617 --> 00:01:33.064
I'm a doctor.

00:01:35.282 --> 00:01:37.667
Please, take a look at this seagull!

00:01:37.721 --> 00:01:40.710
I'm not a vet!
I'm a doctor for people!

00:01:43.279 --> 00:01:48.021
But... don't you know how to treat birds?
It's a living creature, as well!

00:01:48.056 --> 00:01:51.642
Are you making fun of me?
I'm insulted!

00:02:03.867 --> 00:02:08.478
Miss Candice,
let's head back to the cabin.

00:02:09.209 --> 00:02:10.267
But...

00:02:12.842 --> 00:02:16.591
There is a first aid kit in the room.
Now, let's go.

00:02:37.712 --> 00:02:39.687
I've applied this medicine,
so you'll be okay.

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:42.476
You'll have to rest after this.

00:02:43.607 --> 00:02:46.289
But how come you injured yourself?

00:02:46.642 --> 00:02:49.117
Maybe it was attracted by a
reflection from the window.

00:02:49.118 --> 00:02:51.201
It flew towards the window and struck the glass.

00:02:57.475 --> 00:02:58.947
You must have been in pain.

00:03:01.289 --> 00:03:04.226
But I'll make sure you'll be
able to fly again.

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:11.184
Come in.

00:03:12.646 --> 00:03:13.454
Excuse me,

00:03:13.489 --> 00:03:17.827
Candice White, the captain
would like to see you.

00:03:18.018 --> 00:03:19.975
Captain?

00:03:21.386 --> 00:03:23.034
...wants to see me?

00:03:29.387 --> 00:03:30.311
Come in!

00:03:33.242 --> 00:03:38.150
I'm Candice White Adley.
But you can call me Candy.

00:03:39.421 --> 00:03:41.408
I'm captain Wells.

00:03:41.443 --> 00:03:43.858
I hope you're not mad
for calling you out of the blue.

00:03:43.893 --> 00:03:44.482
I'm not!

00:03:44.517 --> 00:03:48.367
First of all, I'd like to express my gratitude.
Thank you.

00:03:50.848 --> 00:03:55.056
You gave my last journey
something to remember it by.

00:03:55.282 --> 00:03:56.773
Last journey?

00:03:57.386 --> 00:04:02.007
That's right. I am going to retire
after this journey.

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:04.886
I will fill in the last page
of the ship's diary...

00:04:04.921 --> 00:04:08.498
...with the story of a kind young
girl who saved a seagull.

00:04:12.603 --> 00:04:14.146
And how is your seagull doing?

00:04:14.186 --> 00:04:17.137
-It's good.
-I'm glad to hear that.

00:04:17.655 --> 00:04:22.092
Now the only thing left is praying
that we safely finish our journey.

00:04:22.995 --> 00:04:27.096
Uh, captain Wells... what are you
going to do after you retire?

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:43.394
I'll take the severance and
settle somewhere near the sea.

00:04:46.508 --> 00:04:48.356
-Captain! Captain!
-What's the matter?

00:04:48.391 --> 00:04:50.668
-We've received a SOS call!
-What?

00:04:50.861 --> 00:04:54.662
Tidal wave overturned a small fishing boat!

00:04:59.511 --> 00:05:01.302
Which ship is closest to them?

00:05:01.510 --> 00:05:02.840
This one.

00:05:03.029 --> 00:05:06.380
We can't just leave them.
I'll command the rescue operations.

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:16.229
So we'll run a day late because the ship
will detour on a rescue operation?

00:05:16.447 --> 00:05:20.618
Stear and Archie will probably be very worried.

00:05:22.262 --> 00:05:24.640
Stear and Archie are waiting for us?

00:05:27.568 --> 00:05:29.592
No! You can't do that!

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:39.446
You can't detour the ship. You can't
do this on your own accord, captain.

00:05:39.685 --> 00:05:43.125
Your job is to get this ship to
England in time.

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:45.660
But... since we received a SOS...

00:05:45.695 --> 00:05:48.481
Some other rescue ship will pick them up.

00:05:48.516 --> 00:05:52.353
Besides, there are other reasons for this.
Come with me.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:57.186
They're here!

00:06:01.667 --> 00:06:02.692
Come in!

00:06:06.157 --> 00:06:08.435
Excuse me!
My name is Stafford.

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:13.310
Wouldn't it be a problem for you
if you didn't get to England in time?

00:06:13.345 --> 00:06:16.669
I'm only a subordinate of miss Candice.

00:06:17.091 --> 00:06:19.017
So you're in charge, right?

00:06:21.354 --> 00:06:25.983
Miss Candice, this is one of the richest
men in the world, mr. Stafford.

00:06:27.115 --> 00:06:31.191
What do you think, miss?
You'd like to arrive as soon as possible, right?

00:06:31.643 --> 00:06:37.393
Yes, but... I'd rather leave everything
to captain Wells.

00:06:40.882 --> 00:06:45.432
I invested a lot into this venture. If we run late,
I'm going to lose a lot of money!

00:06:45.467 --> 00:06:48.344
Unfortunately, I know that lost
human lives can't be recovered.

00:06:48.345 --> 00:06:50.598
We'll come to their rescue.

00:06:51.446 --> 00:06:52.394
Wait!

00:06:52.839 --> 00:06:55.522
Are you going to disregard
my orders, captain Wells?

00:06:55.557 --> 00:06:58.652
I can have you fired!

00:06:59.252 --> 00:07:00.652
Fired?

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:03.800
If I fire you, you and your
career will be done for!

00:07:03.801 --> 00:07:08.247
You'll have a hard time
making a living after this!

00:07:08.248 --> 00:07:09.784
Are you fine with that?

00:07:11.462 --> 00:07:12.462
I am.

00:07:17.148 --> 00:07:20.384
Damn it, I'll show you!

00:07:26.809 --> 00:07:31.442
We're commencing a rescue operation!
Change course to north-east!

00:07:58.298 --> 00:08:01.056
-Captain Wells?
-Oh, Candy.

00:08:01.275 --> 00:08:03.948
The one who enabled you to do this
is right here, I guess.

00:08:05.042 --> 00:08:06.290
That's correct.

00:08:12.138 --> 00:08:15.804
Do you think I'll let you do this?
I'll show you my power!

00:08:16.309 --> 00:08:17.338
Excuse me!

00:08:21.037 --> 00:08:24.384
Did you need something, mr. Stafford?

00:08:25.541 --> 00:08:28.052
Send this telegram. It's urgent.

00:08:29.583 --> 00:08:31.085
As you wish.

00:08:35.679 --> 00:08:39.901
That's right! The view from up
here is excellent!

00:08:40.633 --> 00:08:47.241
Yes... but captain, you said that you
wanted your last journey to pass uneventfully.

00:08:48.294 --> 00:08:51.515
That's right. But just look how
hectic it's become now!

00:08:56.927 --> 00:09:01.406
But... I think you should get a medal
for carrying out this rescue operation.

00:09:02.287 --> 00:09:06.262
You too, for saving that seagull.

00:09:08.797 --> 00:09:12.972
Captain!
This message just came in from headquarters!

00:09:13.225 --> 00:09:14.960
What does it say?

00:09:15.168 --> 00:09:18.911
No need to detour to the accident site.
Return immediately.

00:09:19.322 --> 00:09:22.294
Mr. Stafford is the largest shareholder.

00:09:22.714 --> 00:09:24.317
You are to follow his orders.

00:09:24.539 --> 00:09:27.330
Mr. Stafford must have informed
the headquarters.

00:09:28.389 --> 00:09:29.477
What will you do?

00:09:31.612 --> 00:09:33.609
They'll fire me if I
don't follow their orders, eh?

00:09:42.156 --> 00:09:44.380
Same course, full speed ahead!

00:09:59.255 --> 00:10:01.306
-Miss Candice.
-George.

00:10:02.566 --> 00:10:06.484
Captain Wells is going on a rescue
mission which will get him fired.

00:10:07.015 --> 00:10:08.887
-He's a great man.
-Yes.

00:10:09.563 --> 00:10:11.710
But I wonder what will happen
to him after he gets fired.

00:10:12.723 --> 00:10:18.250
Because he disregarded orders given to him,
he probably won't get his severance pay.

00:10:18.442 --> 00:10:20.108
The punishment will be that bad?

00:10:20.434 --> 00:10:23.968
Yes. He didn't follow orders from
the headquarters.

00:10:24.003 --> 00:10:29.202
In that case, the only thing he'll own
will be the ship's diary full of memories!

00:10:30.344 --> 00:10:33.789
They will probably confiscate
the diary and fire him.

00:10:39.101 --> 00:10:43.112
That's horrible!
He's doing a good thing, isn't he?

00:10:43.550 --> 00:10:47.131
-I won't let that happen!
-Miss Candice!

00:10:54.185 --> 00:10:56.886
*Denjin Anime Fansub*
We're back, and with a bad filler episode, too!

00:11:03.266 --> 00:11:05.535
-Mr. Stafford!
-What is it?

00:11:06.967 --> 00:11:09.548
Having Captain fired is unfair!

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:13.138
If he doesn't want that to happen;

00:11:14.965 --> 00:11:17.910
...he'd better get this ship
to England in time.

00:11:17.945 --> 00:11:21.511
It's his obligation to all the passengers.

00:11:43.311 --> 00:11:45.222
It's so bright!

00:11:47.614 --> 00:11:49.894
I think we've changed course...

00:11:50.384 --> 00:11:51.523
Maybe...?

00:11:56.092 --> 00:11:59.213
It's okay. We're going directly
towards them.

00:11:59.436 --> 00:12:02.239
I wonder will those people be okay.

00:12:12.024 --> 00:12:14.542
30 degrees to starboard!
Engines full speed ahead!

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:20.335
-Take a look.
-Yes.

00:12:28.384 --> 00:12:29.835
-There they are!
-Where?

00:12:29.870 --> 00:12:31.313
Over there!

00:12:33.025 --> 00:12:35.760
We got them!
Commence the operation!

00:12:45.196 --> 00:12:48.130
-A ship!
-A ship!

00:12:52.779 --> 00:12:55.199
-They are waving to us!
-Lower the boat!

00:13:07.834 --> 00:13:13.066
Be careful! If you get overturned,
you're done for! Hold on tightly!

00:13:30.629 --> 00:13:33.105
Alright. It's okay now.

00:13:49.768 --> 00:13:51.398
Thank you!

00:13:54.573 --> 00:13:59.520
-Is everyone okay?
-Thank you!

00:13:59.883 --> 00:14:02.254
Good. Very good.

00:14:06.521 --> 00:14:08.296
Captain Wells is crying.

00:14:08.858 --> 00:14:10.858
He's moved to the point of crying.

00:14:18.504 --> 00:14:22.048
Everyone, thank you for your
cooperation.

00:14:22.083 --> 00:14:25.675
We successfully saved all fishermen.

00:14:54.018 --> 00:14:55.445
Yes, come in!

00:14:55.877 --> 00:14:57.500
Captain Wells.

00:14:57.810 --> 00:14:59.920
It's because I'll be dismissed
as soon as we get to England.

00:15:00.147 --> 00:15:02.146
I'm packing up while I have time.

00:15:04.228 --> 00:15:08.134
All of these things are my keepsakes.

00:15:09.022 --> 00:15:11.617
-What about that photo?
-That's my son.

00:15:11.984 --> 00:15:15.580
So you'll be living with him from now on?

00:15:18.894 --> 00:15:20.629
My son is dead.

00:15:22.971 --> 00:15:26.867
The sea...
My son was a sailor.

00:15:26.902 --> 00:15:30.124
One day, his ship got overturned...

00:15:32.612 --> 00:15:35.262
...and he never came back after that.

00:15:39.243 --> 00:15:45.008
And so, this photo became the only thing that
could lessen my loneliness during voyages.

00:15:57.530 --> 00:16:00.380
What is it?
Barging in without knocking!

00:16:00.644 --> 00:16:03.747
Mr. Stafford, have you ever loved somebody?

00:16:03.782 --> 00:16:05.422
You have some nerve!

00:16:05.612 --> 00:16:10.392
Do you have any idea how hard it is
when you lose somebody you love?

00:16:23.163 --> 00:16:26.372
The son of captain Wells died at sea.

00:16:26.407 --> 00:16:32.908
If somebody truly knows the value
of a human life, it's captain Wells.

00:16:33.554 --> 00:16:36.979
That's why he couldn't have
abandoned those people.

00:16:37.415 --> 00:16:42.292
I, too, know how it feels to lose
a beloved person.

00:16:48.165 --> 00:16:50.782
Lost money can return eventually,

00:16:52.018 --> 00:16:55.586
...but once a human life is lost...

00:16:57.768 --> 00:16:59.253
...it can't return.

00:17:01.405 --> 00:17:06.661
And you wanted to stop Captain from saving
so many lives with that single telegram!

00:17:11.777 --> 00:17:13.334
That is so wrong!

00:17:16.975 --> 00:17:18.275
Wrong!

00:17:18.815 --> 00:17:20.123
Wrong!

00:17:38.372 --> 00:17:42.530
I can't give you any strength.
I'm sorry.

00:17:42.876 --> 00:17:49.786
It's okay, Candy. If this seagull is
fine, I'll be fine as well.

00:17:52.067 --> 00:17:54.007
Now, set it free.

00:17:54.960 --> 00:17:57.242
Okay? Don't push yourself too hard.

00:17:57.277 --> 00:17:59.476
If you don't have enough strength,
you can come back.

00:18:09.585 --> 00:18:11.239
It flew!

00:18:20.936 --> 00:18:22.903
Farewell!

00:18:23.206 --> 00:18:30.788
-Won't you all gather in the great hall?
-In the great hall? What for?

00:18:30.997 --> 00:18:35.101
It's a party in honor of captain Wells's
last journey!

00:18:35.546 --> 00:18:36.903
Mr. Stafford!

00:18:39.307 --> 00:18:40.920
We'll be waiting for you.

00:18:51.925 --> 00:18:53.265
Cheers!

00:18:55.917 --> 00:18:58.241
-Congratulations, captain.
-Thank you.

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:06.161
Captain Wells, congratulations
on your last journey.

00:19:06.755 --> 00:19:08.497
Thank you, Candy.

00:19:08.546 --> 00:19:14.207
Thank you, everyone! I will remember
this happiness for a very long time!

00:19:15.231 --> 00:19:17.190
I am so fortunate.

00:19:30.115 --> 00:19:31.300
Cheers!

00:19:31.301 --> 00:19:34.813
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

00:19:43.137 --> 00:19:47.319
Miss Candice, you'll get sick if
you drink too much champagne.

00:19:48.429 --> 00:19:51.011
No, that's not it... it's...

00:19:52.431 --> 00:19:54.682
What'll I do... I guess I really
had too much.

00:20:12.551 --> 00:20:13.977
What a fog!

00:20:18.687 --> 00:20:21.497
England... I wonder what it's alike.

00:20:22.277 --> 00:20:25.221
I'll get to meet more wonderful
people, just like captain Wells!

00:20:25.256 --> 00:20:26.912
I'm glad I came!

00:20:27.629 --> 00:20:29.776
I wonder if Stear and Archie are
waiting for me.

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:33.886
If I'll be together with those two,
any place could be wonderful.

00:20:58.293 --> 00:21:00.142
Anthony?

00:21:02.889 --> 00:21:07.384
Candy saw Anthony's image in the dense fog.

00:21:08.211 --> 00:21:10.201
Was it an illusion?

00:21:11.094 --> 00:21:14.314
London is almost a stone-throw away.

00:21:15.291 --> 00:21:19.222
To be continued...
